From b015c287ec58d46abecc9a10f045d66f89f90cdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:21:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): supervisor-request retry_limit op [daveey]

A worker that created a flaky card had no supported route to widen its retry
breaker after creation: the worker shell is fenced from 'hermes kanban edit'
and kanban_supervisor_request only had link/unlink/reconcile_notify/resume.

New op {op: retry_limit, task_id, max_retries 1-10} (bools refused), its own
request family. Scope: only a live card the requester created, never the
requester's own card (self_scope), never archived/done targets. The non-worker
executor re-checks scope and the requester at execution, applies through
kanban_db_operator.edit_operator_fields only (one 'edited' event), reports
old/new/readback, and marks the target with a supervisor_retry_limit event so
a redelivered request reports already_applied instead of writing twice.
kanban_create's cap now comes from the same MAX_RETRY_LIMIT.
---
